<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/249126> <https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/dspace/dc.date.accessioned> "2015-05-21T04:39:27Z" <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/249126> <https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/dspace/dc.date.accessioned> "2016-08-08T06:07:24Z" <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/249154> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "Tuberculosis remains a major global public health challenge, and the WHO End TB Strategy emphasizes the need for early diagnosis and universal drug-susceptibility testing. This policy guidance presents evidence-based recommendations on the use of the commercial loop-mediated isothermal amplification assay (TB-LAMP) for the diagnosis of pulmonary tuberculosis. Developed following a systematic review of studies conducted since 2012 and assessment using the GRADE approach, the document evaluates the diagnostic accuracy of TB-LAMP as a replacement for sputum-smear microscopy, as an add-on test after negative smear microscopy, and in comparison with the Xpert MTB/RIF assay, while also assessing the frequency of indeterminate or invalid results.\n\nBased on the available evidence, WHO recommends that TB-LAMP may be used as a replacement for sputum-smear microscopy in adults with signs and symptoms of pulmonary tuberculosis and as a follow-on test when further investigation of smear-negative specimens is required. The guidance emphasizes that these conditional recommendations are based on very low-quality evidence, apply to sputum specimens from patients with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis, and should not replace rapid molecular tests capable of detecting rifampicin resistance. It also highlights the limited evidence for use in people living with HIV, notes the extrapolation of recommendations to children, and provides implementation considerations and priorities for future research." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/249154> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/available> "2016-08-08T13:52:14Z"^^<http://purl.org/dc/terms/W3CDTF> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
