<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/375059> <https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/dspace/dc.rights.uri> "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/igo"@en-us <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/375230> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "This second edition of the digital adaptation kit for HIV provides operational, software-neutral requirements to support the incorporation of WHO clinical, public health and data use recommendations into digital systems. Developed within the SMART Guidelines approach, it focuses on the content requirements for person-centred digital tracking and decision support systems used by health workers for HIV services in primary health care settings. The kit is intended to facilitate transparent, consistent and adaptable translation of narrative guidance into digital implementations while supporting interoperability and local customization.\n\nThe publication organizes HIV-related requirements into eight components: health interventions and associated recommendations; generic personas; illustrative user scenarios; business processes and workflows; core data elements; decision support and scheduling logic; indicators and performance metrics; and high-level functional and non-functional requirements. It covers processes including HIV testing, pre-exposure prophylaxis, care and treatment, prevention of mother-to-child transmission, infant diagnosis, diagnostics, client follow-up, referral, and aggregate reporting and data use, with complementary operational resources provided in web annexes." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
