<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/58534> <https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/dspace/dc.subject.meshqualifier> "therapy"@en <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://hdl.handle.net/10665/59577> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "These guidelines provide recommendations for preventing and controlling infection with LAV/HTLV-III, the retrovirus recognized at the time as the etiological agent of acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS). Developed as part of the WHO AIDS Control Programme, they are intended primarily for public health authorities and health professionals, who are responsible for adapting the guidance to different populations and settings. The document summarizes available knowledge on transmission, clinical manifestations, laboratory detection, surveillance, notification and confidentiality, and case definitions for AIDS.\n\nThe guidelines emphasize routine precautions to prevent exposure to blood and other potentially infectious body fluids, particularly among health care workers, laboratory personnel and providers of home and emergency care. They address prevention and management of needlestick, parenteral and mucous-membrane exposures, safe handling of specimens and contaminated equipment, and precautions for non-health-care workers. Guidance is also provided on disinfection, sterilization, and the safe processing of reusable needles, syringes and other instruments." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
