<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/10665-97885.sec-023.45> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Although five of the six studies had higher vaccine effectiveness for two doses compared to one dose, only one study reached statistical significance, and this was probably due to the large sample size (Cohen et al., 2007). Despite relatively high two-dose vaccine effectiveness, high two-dose vaccine coverage may not be sufficient to prevent all outbreaks (Cortese et al., 2008; Dayan & Rubin, 2008)." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/10665-97885.sec-023.45> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2008"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
