<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-057.6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Amino acids The three-letter symbols in the table opposite may be used for repre-senting polymers or sequences and in figures and tables; a known sequence of amino acids is indicated by hyphens between the symbols. The use of one-letter symbols should be restricted to the comparison of long sequences. T Recently renamed the International Union of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (IUBMB)." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
