<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-061.6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Drugs and pesticides For pharmaceuticals the International Nonproprietary Names (INNs) should be used, and for pesticides the common names adopted by the International Organization for Standardization (see International Stan-dard ISO 1750:1981, and subsequent addenda and amendments). When no internationally approved name exists, an approved national name may be used. Proprietary names should be avoided whenever possible." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
