<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-062.3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Oncogenes Oncogenes are usually designated by three-letter italic terms, often taken from the names of the viruses with which the genes are WHO Editorial Style Manual associated. A roman prefix may be added: “v-” for viral, “N-” for nuclear and “c-” for the gene’s cellular counterpart (proto-oncogene). Other prefixes and various suffixes are common. For example: Ha-ras-1 N-ras v-erb B yes c-abl fes/fps." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-062.3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/Work> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063-2.1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Issit PD, Crookston MC. Blood group terminology: current conventions. Trans-fusion, 1984, 24:2-7." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063-2.1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "1984"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063-2.1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/Work> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063-2.2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Clfting factors Clotting factors are usually designated by roman numerals (¢.g. factor IX). An “a” added to the numeral indicates the activated form of the factor (e.g. factor VIIa)." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063-2.2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/Work> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063.1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Smith HO, Nathans D. A suggested nomenclature for bacterial host modification and restriction systems and their enzymes. Journal of molecular biology, 1973, 81:419-423." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063.1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "1973"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
