<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063.3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Clfting factors Clotting factors are usually designated by roman numerals (¢.g. factor IX). An “a” added to the numeral indicates the activated form of the factor (e.g. factor VIIa)." <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-063.3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/Work> <https://iris.who.int/graph/metadata> .
